From 6ef4f5a42e8b445798eda33f63476a5bd64585e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: codEx Fork Bot <codex-fork-bot@localhost>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 01:18:58 +0800
Subject: interaction: /rewind rollback and double-Esc interrupt

Adds /rewind: a searchable picker rolls the conversation back by forking
the thread before the selected message (restoring its prompt to the
composer) and optionally restores workspace files from plain snapshots
taken before each turn (~/.codex/snapshots/<workspace>/<turn>/, no git
involved, gitignore-aware, incremental, capped at 20). The old main-view
Esc-Esc backtrack is removed in favor of /rewind.

Esc interaction is rebuilt: a single Esc is a no-op, a second Esc within
400ms while a reply runs stops it, and chat.interrupt_turn is unbound by
default. Contexts that already own Esc (modals, popups, overlays, vim
insert mode, bash prompts) keep their behavior.

Also fixes two rollback bugs: the previous thread transcript is cleared
before the forked thread is attached so the old conversation no longer
remains visible, and the message picker maps the 0-based message ordinal
to snapshot index nth + 1 (snapshots are numbered from 1) so files are
restored to the state before the selected turn. Adds an end-to-end
regression test covering the fork, transcript truncation, composer
restore, and file snapshot restore.
